# The question tool's menu at 24 columns, as claude 2.1.259 draws it. Two long
# descriptions push the box's top and the first choice's marker above the rows a
# rule may see, while the bottom stays. The footer wraps into three rows,
# leaving `Enter to select` on the first and splitting `Esc to cancel`.
print ────────────────────────
print  ☐ Indentation
print
print Should this project be
print indented with spaces or
print tabs?
print
print ❯ 1. Spaces
print      Fixed-width
print      indentation that
print      renders identically
print      everywhere; the
print      common default for
print      most language style
print      guides and
print      formatters.
print   2. Tabs
print      One tab character
print      per level, so each
print      reader's editor
print      controls the
print      visible width;
print      better for
print      accessibility and
print      smaller files.
print   3. Type something.
print ────────────────────────
print   4. Chat about this
print
print Enter to select · ↑/↓ to
print navigate · Esc to
print cancel
# The menu waits for an answer.
sleep 600000
